env
- print the environment
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
env
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Env writes the environment it inherited to the standard output, one
name=value string per line, in the order the vector gives them.
.sp
It takes no arguments and changes nothing.  A program started with
exec(2) has an empty environment and prints nothing; execve(2), or a
shell that exports variables, is what puts anything there.
.sp 2
.in -5
